# The version to release, as X.N.V.M. Writing a new one here and pushing to
# main is what cuts a release: tag.yml watches this file, checks that ci and
# compat are green for the commit, tags it, and builds a draft release.
#
# It has to match the version in pyproject.toml at the commit that changes it,
# so the last commit of a series bumps both. Between releases this names the
# last one cut, which is normally behind the version being worked on.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored. The first line that is
# neither is the version.

0.1.6.5
